<title>USA: TECO Energy leases Kentucky coal reserves.</title>
<headline>TECO Energy leases Kentucky coal reserves.</headline>
<dateline>TAMPA, Fla. 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>TECO Energy Inc said on Wednesday its TECO Coal Corp subsidiary leased the mining rights to about 10 million tons of coal reserves in eastern Kentucky.</p>
<p>The reserves, in Pike and Floyd counties, are contiguous to TECO's Premier Elkhorn operation, and the transaction includes the right to use railroad facilities that will add about one million tons to Premier Elkhorn's production capacity, TECO said.</p>
<p>TECO will lease the reserves from ANR Coal Co LLC, a subsidiary of Coastal Corp.</p>
